- C uses braces { } to define the beginning and end of blocks of code, whereas Fortran uses do/end do blocks.
- C uses the `for` loop syntax with the `<=` operator to iterate over a range of integers, whereas Fortran uses the `do` loop syntax with a comma-separated range of values.
