{"role": "assistant", "content": "If the widget you bind in your targeting widget appears to be null, it might be because the widget is not initialized or accessed incorrectly. Here's a checklist to help you identify the issue:

1. Make sure the widget class reference is set in the constructor or in Defaults in the Blueprint. If you're using C++, set the class reference in the constructor of your AGameplayAbilityTargetActor_GroundTrace:

```cpp
