{"role": "assistant", "content": "Sure, here's an implementation of the `Expr` class and the `Compiler` visitor in `backend.kt`:

```kotlin
sealed class Expr {
    data class Num(val value: Int): Expr()
    data class Str(val value: String): Expr()
    data class Var(val name: String): Expr()
    data class BinOp(val op: String, val left: Expr, val right: Expr): Expr()
    data class FunCall(val name: String, val args: List<Expr>): Expr()
    data class Assign(val name: String, val value: Expr): Expr()
    data class ForLoop(val id: String, val start: Expr, val end: Expr, val body: Expr): Expr()
}

class Compiler : PLBaseVisitor<Expr>() {
    override fun visitProgram(ctx: PLParser.ProgramContext): Expr {
        return Expr.Block(ctx.statement().map { visit(it) })
    }

    override fun visitAssignment(ctx: PLParser.AssignmentContext): Expr {
        return Expr.Assign(ctx.ID().text, visit(ctx.expr()))
    }

    override fun visitNum(ctx: PLParser.NumContext): Expr {
        return Expr.Num(ctx.text.toInt())
    }

    override fun visitStr(ctx: PLParser.StrContext): Expr {
        return Expr.Str(ctx.text.substring(1, ctx.text.length - 1))
    }

    override fun visitVar(ctx: PLParser.VarContext): Expr {
        return Expr.Var(ctx.ID().text)
    }

    override fun visitBinOp(ctx: PLParser.BinOpContext): Expr {
        val op = ctx.op.text
        val left = visit(ctx.left)
        val right = visit(ctx.right)
        return Expr.BinOp(op, left, right)
    }

    override fun visitPrint(ctx: PLParser.PrintContext): Expr {
        return Expr.Print(visit(ctx.expr()))
    }

    override fun visitFunction_definition(ctx: PLParser.Function_definitionContext): Expr {
        val argNames = ctx.function_params().ID().map { it.text }
        val body = ctx.statement().map { visit(it) }
        return Expr.FunctionDefinition(ctx.ID().text, argNames, body)
    }

    override fun visitFunction_call(ctx: PLParser.Function_callContext): Expr {
        val functionName = ctx.ID().text
        val args = ctx.function_call_params()?.expr()?.map { visit(it) } ?: emptyList()
        return Expr.FunctionCall(functionName, args)
    }

    override fun visitFor_loop(ctx: PLParser.For_loopContext): Expr {
        val id = ctx.ID().text
        val start = visit(ctx.expr(0))
        val end = visit(ctx.expr(1))
        val body = visit(ctx.statement())
        return Expr.ForLoop(id, start, end, body)
    }
}
```

The `Expr` class represents the various expressions that can be evaluated in the PL language. The `Compiler` class is a visitor that traverses the parse tree generated by ANTLR4 and constructs the corresponding `Expr` objects.

The `visit` methods in the `Compiler` class are callbacks that are called by the ANTLR4 parser when a specific rule in the grammar is matched. The `visitProgram` method generates a block of statements from a sequence of program statements. The `visitAssignment`, `visitNum`, `visitStr`, `visitVar`, `visitBinOp`, `visitPrint`, `visitFunction_definition`, `visitFunction_call`, and `visitFor_loop` methods generate the corresponding `Expr` objects from their respective parse tree nodes.

Note that this implementation is not complete, and you may need to add more functionality based on the specific requirements of the SDD and the backend implementation."},
