{"role": "assistant", "content": "Alright, then let's modify the `VueClient` class to display the list of available flights from the airline company's repository, instead of using a hardcoded list of flights:

```java
import java.util.List;
import javax.swing.*;

public class VueClient extends JFrame implements Observer {
    private JLabel lblAeroportDepart;
    private JLabel lblDateDepart;
    private JComboBox<String> cmbAeroportDepart;
    private JTextField txtDateDepart;
    private JButton btnRechercher;
    private JTable tblVols;

    private List<Vol> vols;

    public VueClient() {
        super("Client");

        // initialize components
        lblAeroportDepart = new JLabel("Aéroport de départ:");
        lblDateDepart = new JLabel("Date de départ:");
        cmbAeroportDepart = new JComboBox<>();
        txtDateDepart = new JTextField(10);
        btnRechercher = new JButton("Rechercher");
        tblVols = new JTable();

        // add components to panel
        JPanel panel = new JPanel();
        panel.add(lblAeroportDepart);
        panel.add(cmbAeroportDepart);
        panel.add(lblDateDepart);
        panel.add(txtDateDepart);
        panel.add(btnRechercher);
        panel.add(new JScrollPane(tblVols));

        // add panel to frame
        add(panel);

        // set frame properties
        setDefaultCloseOperation(JFrame.DISPOSE_ON_CLOSE);
        pack();
        setLocationRelativeTo(null);

        // initialize combo box with airport names
        cmbAeroportDepart.addItem("Paris");
        cmbAeroportDepart.addItem("New York");
        cmbAeroportDepart.addItem("Tokyo");

        // register as observer for vol updates
        Aeroport.getInstance().registerObserver(this);

        // initial vol update
        update();

        // add listener to search button
        btnRechercher.addActionListener(e -> {
            String aeroportDepart = (String) cmbAeroportDepart.getSelectedItem();
            String dateDepart = txtDateDepart.getText();
            updateVols(aeroportDepart, dateDepart);
        });
    }

    public void update() {
        vols = Aeroport.getInstance().getVols();
        String aeroportDepart = (String) cmbAeroportDepart.getSelectedItem();
        String dateDepart = txtDateDepart.getText();

        // display vols in table
        DefaultTableModel model = new DefaultTableModel();
        model.addColumn("Vol");
        model.addColumn("Départ");
        model.addColumn("Arrivée");
        model.addColumn("Compagnie");
        model.addColumn("Cabines");
        for (Vol vol : vols) {
            if (vol.getAeroportDepart().equals(aeroportDepart) && vol.getDateDepart().equals(dateDepart)) {
                // flight matches search criteria, add to table
                model.addRow(new Object[] {
                    vol.getCodeVol(),
                    vol.getAeroportDepart(),
                    vol.getAeroportArrivee(),
                    vol.getCompagnie(),
                    vol.getNbCabines()
                });
            }
        }
        tblVols.setModel(model);
    }

    private void updateVols(String aeroportDepart, String dateDepart) {
        // update vol list based on search criteria
        List<Vol> vols = Aeroport.getInstance().chercherVols(aeroportDepart, dateDepart);
        refresher(vols);
    }

    public void refresher(List<Vol> vols) {
        this.vols.clear();
        this.vols.addAll(vols);
        update();
    } 
}
```

This updated version of `VueClient` now uses the `Aeroport` class to retrieve the list of flights, and displays them in a table. The `update()` method updates the table whenever there is a change to the list of flights, and the `updateVols()` method retrieves the list of flights based on the user's search criteria (departure airport and date), and calls the `refresher()` method to update the table view with the new search results."},
